    "file": "ecosystem/index.html",
    "title": "Supporting Instruments | MIZAN",
    "description": "Qudra, Mu'tamad, Isnad and Misbar as supporting instruments for MIZAN approval cases.",
    "ogTitle": "Supporting Instruments | MIZAN",
    "ogDescription": "Qudra, Mu'tamad, Isnad and Misbar as supporting instruments for MIZAN approval cases.",
    "canonical": "https://mizangov.com/ecosystem/",
    "bodyClass": "",
    "mainHtml": "<section class=\"page-hero\"><div class=\"container\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Supporting instruments</div><h1>Supporting the people and evidence behind the decision</h1><p class=\"support\">MIZAN's wider research and development programme includes four supporting instruments. Their role is to strengthen an approval case for a specific AI use. Availability and pilot scope should be agreed with the team.</p></div></section><section class=\"section\"><div class=\"container\"><div class=\"section-kicker\">Four instruments</div><h2 class=\"section-heading medium\">Secondary tools, not a competing front door</h2><div class=\"grid-4\" style=\"margin-top:28px\"><article class=\"instrument-card\"><h3>Qudra</h3><p><strong>Institutional capability.</strong> Examines whether the organisation has the mandate, people, processes and supervision needed for this AI use.</p><p><a class=\"inline-link\" href=\"/qudra/\">Explore capability</a></p></article><article class=\"instrument-card\"><h3>Mu'tamad</h3><p><strong>Human competence.</strong> Defines and assesses the knowledge and skills required of named reviewers and supervisors.</p><p><a class=\"inline-link\" href=\"/mutamad/\">Explore accountable roles</a></p></article><article class=\"instrument-card\"><h3>Isnad</h3><p><strong>Evidence and knowledge provenance.</strong> Records where knowledge and evidence came from, who reviewed it, and when it needs updating.</p><p><a class=\"inline-link\" href=\"/isnad/\">Explore evidence sources</a></p></article><article class=\"instrument-card\"><h3>Misbar</h3><p><strong>Controlled research.</strong> Tests assumptions, boundaries and failure scenarios in a defined environment before wider use.</p><p><a class=\"inline-link\" href=\"/misbar/\">Explore research testing</a></p></article></div></div></section>"
