  "/how-it-works/": {
    "route": "/how-it-works/",
    "file": "how-it-works/index.html",
    "title": "How It Works | MIZAN",
    "description": "The six-step MIZAN workflow for evidence-backed AI approval decisions.",
    "ogTitle": "How It Works | MIZAN",
    "ogDescription": "The six-step MIZAN workflow for evidence-backed AI approval decisions.",
    "canonical": "https://mizangov.com/how-it-works/",
    "bodyClass": "",
    "mainHtml": "<section class=\"page-hero\"><div class=\"container\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">How it works</div><h1>From evidence to accountable authorisation</h1><p class=\"support\">The same six steps appear across the site: Define, Evidence, Assess, Authorise, Monitor and Reauthorise. The worked example below follows a student support assistant (constructed).</p></div></section>\n      <section class=\"section\" aria-labelledby=\"steps-title\"><div class=\"container\"><div class=\"section-kicker\">Six-step workflow</div><h2 id=\"steps-title\" class=\"section-heading medium\">The human decision point stays visible</h2><div class=\"grid-3\" style=\"margin-top:28px\"><article class=\"card\"><span class=\"status-tag\">Step 1</span><h3>Define</h3><p><strong>What you bring:</strong> Purpose, owner, permitted actions and limits.</p><p><strong>Who is involved:</strong> Service owner and governance lead.</p><p><strong>What MIZAN produces:</strong> A bounded use case and draft approval scope.</p></article><article class=\"card\"><span class=\"status-tag\">Step 2</span><h3>Evidence</h3><p><strong>What you bring:</strong> Policies, privacy review, security review, accessibility testing and source list.</p><p><strong>Who is involved:</strong> Evidence owners and specialist teams.</p><p><strong>What MIZAN produces:</strong> A connected evidence set with source and review status.</p></article><article class=\"card\"><span class=\"status-tag\">Step 3</span><h3>Assess</h3><p><strong>What you bring:</strong> The connected evidence set and identified gaps.</p><p><strong>Who is involved:</strong> Relevant specialists and accountable reviewers.</p><p><strong>What MIZAN produces:</strong> Findings, unresolved gaps and required conditions.</p></article><article class=\"card\"><span class=\"status-tag\">Step 4</span><h3>Authorise</h3><p><strong>What you bring:</strong> Specialist findings and proposed conditions.</p><p><strong>Who is involved:</strong> An authorised institutional decision owner.</p><p><strong>What MIZAN produces:</strong> A worded decision, reasons, conditions and review date.</p></article><article class=\"card\"><span class=\"status-tag\">Step 5</span><h3>Monitor</h3><p><strong>What you bring:</strong> Agreed signals such as source changes, incidents and complaints.</p><p><strong>Who is involved:</strong> Operational owner with escalation routes.</p><p><strong>What MIZAN produces:</strong> Signals attached to the relevant part of the approval.</p></article><article class=\"card\"><span class=\"status-tag\">Step 6</span><h3>Reauthorise</h3><p><strong>What you bring:</strong> Affected evidence and change history.</p><p><strong>Who is involved:</strong> Decision owner with relevant reviewers.</p><p><strong>What MIZAN produces:</strong> Continue, restrict, suspend or withdraw the approval.</p></article></div></div></section>\n      <section class=\"section light\" aria-labelledby=\"example-workflow-title\"><div class=\"container case-layout\"><div><div class=\"section-kicker\">Worked example</div><h2 id=\"example-workflow-title\" class=\"section-heading medium\">Student support assistant (constructed)</h2><p class=\"section-lede\">The worked example shows how evidence, boundaries and review triggers become an approval record for one AI use.</p><div class=\"hero-actions\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"/contact/\">Discuss a pilot</a></div></div><article class=\"record-card\" aria-label=\"Illustrative education approval record extract\">\n  <p class=\"record-caption\">Illustrative concept using sample information. It does not represent a live deployment.</p>\n  <h3>Approval record extract</h3>\n  <dl class=\"record-list\">\n    <dt>AI use</dt><dd>Student support assistant for routine questions.</dd>\n    <dt>Purpose</dt><dd>Answer questions using approved institutional information.</dd>\n    <dt>Accountable owner</dt><dd>Student services lead.</dd>\n    <dt>Allowed</dt><dd>Use approved sources and draft support responses.</dd>\n    <dt>Not allowed</dt><dd>Decide eligibility, discipline, progression or access to services.</dd>\n    <dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Source accuracy, student data protections, accessibility, staff readiness.</dd>\n    <dt>Decision</dt><dd><span class=\"decision-chip\">Authorised, with conditions</span></dd>\n    <dt>Conditions</dt><dd>Escalate ambiguous questions and consequential decisions to staff.</dd>\n    <dt>Review date</dt><dd>30 January 2027.</dd>\n  </dl>\n</article></div></section>\n      <section class=\"section\" aria-labelledby=\"change-title\"><div class=\"container split-grid\"><div><div class=\"section-kicker\">Material change</div><h2 id=\"change-title\" class=\"section-heading medium\">When the use changes, the permission comes back for review</h2><p class=\"section-lede\">If the assistant is proposed to start making eligibility decisions, the original guidance-only approval must be reassessed. The affected evidence, human decision boundary and accountable owner return to review before any new approval is recorded.</p></div><div class=\"note-card\"><h3>Possible outcomes</h3><p>Continue, restrict, suspend or withdraw the approval. The outcome is recorded in words with the reason and review date, not as a score.</p></div></div></section>"
  },
