  "/platform/": {
    "route": "/platform/",
    "file": "platform/index.html",
    "title": "Platform | MIZAN",
    "description": "One record for evidence, approval and review of institutional AI use.",
    "ogTitle": "Platform | MIZAN",
    "ogDescription": "One record for evidence, approval and review of institutional AI use.",
    "canonical": "https://mizangov.com/platform/",
    "bodyClass": "",
    "mainHtml": "<section class=\"page-hero\" aria-labelledby=\"platform-title\"><div class=\"container hero-grid\"><div class=\"hero-copy\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Platform</div><h1 id=\"platform-title\">One record for evidence, approval and review</h1><p class=\"support\">MIZAN is being developed to help institutions connect an AI use to the evidence, people and conditions that support its approval. The record is designed to stay reviewable as the system and its operating environment change.</p><div class=\"hero-actions\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"/contact/\">Discuss your requirements</a><a class=\"button secondary\" href=\"/how-it-works/\">See the example workflow</a></div></div><article class=\"record-card\" aria-label=\"Illustrative public service decision record\">\n  <p class=\"record-caption\">Illustrative concept using sample information. It does not represent a live deployment.</p>\n  <h3>Resident service assistant (constructed)</h3>\n  <dl class=\"record-list\">\n    <dt>AI use</dt><dd>Resident-facing service assistant.</dd>\n    <dt>Purpose</dt><dd>Explain published requirements and route complex cases to staff.</dd>\n    <dt>Accountable owner</dt><dd>Service delivery director.</dd>\n    <dt>Allowed</dt><dd>Explain guidance, prepare drafts, route cases.</dd>\n    <dt>Not allowed</dt><dd>Make eligibility decisions or change official records.</dd>\n    <dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Service policy, privacy and security review, accessibility testing, answer quality.</dd>\n    <dt>Decision</dt><dd><span class=\"decision-chip\">Authorised, with conditions</span></dd>\n    <dt>Conditions</dt><dd>Staff review ambiguous cases; complaints trigger review.</dd>\n    <dt>Review date</dt><dd>30 January 2027.</dd>\n  </dl>\n</article></div></section>\n      <section class=\"section\" id=\"capabilities\" aria-labelledby=\"capabilities-title\"><div class=\"container\"><div class=\"section-kicker\">Core capabilities</div><h2 id=\"capabilities-title\" class=\"section-heading medium\">What the platform helps you check and record</h2><div class=\"grid-3\" style=\"margin-top:28px\"><article class=\"card\"><h3>Define the approval.</h3><p>Record the purpose, responsible owner, permitted actions, limits and review date.</p></article><article class=\"card\"><h3>Connect the evidence.</h3><p>Link policies, assessments and technical reports to the question each item supports.</p></article><article class=\"card\"><h3>Record specialist review.</h3><p>Keep specialist findings, unresolved gaps and required conditions visible to the decision owner.</p></article><article class=\"card\"><h3>Check organisational capability.</h3><p>Assess mandate, people, processes, data controls, supervision, transparency, contestability and monitoring for this use.</p></article><article class=\"card\"><h3>Review changes.</h3><p>Connect agreed change signals to the parts of the approval that need reassessment.</p></article><article class=\"card\"><h3>Recover the history.</h3><p>Show what was known, what was reviewed, who decided, and the conditions attached.</p></article></div></div></section>\n      <section class=\"section light\" aria-labelledby=\"systems-title\"><div class=\"container split-grid\"><div><div class=\"section-kicker\">Working with existing systems</div><h2 id=\"systems-title\" class=\"section-heading medium\">Designed to use the evidence institutions already hold</h2><p class=\"section-lede\">MIZAN is designed to use evidence from existing risk, privacy, security and AI evaluation processes. Integration and deployment requirements should be agreed for each pilot, including identity, permissions, hosting, data access and change monitoring.</p></div><div class=\"grid-2\"><article class=\"note-card\"><span class=\"status-tag\">Available now</span><h3>Structured approval record</h3><p>Manual evidence mapping and review fields for focused pilot use.</p></article><article class=\"note-card\"><span class=\"status-tag\">In development</span><h3>Evidence import workflow</h3><p>Connector requirements to be agreed during pilot scoping.</p></article><article class=\"note-card\"><span class=\"status-tag\">Planned</span><h3>Change monitoring signals</h3><p>Signal design depends on deployed systems and permissions.</p></article><article class=\"note-card\"><span class=\"status-tag\">Planned</span><h3>Identity and permissions</h3><p>Deployment-specific integration, not presented as live today.</p></article></div></div></section>\n      <section class=\"section\" id=\"governance-comparison\" aria-labelledby=\"comparison-title\"><div class=\"container\"><div class=\"section-kicker\">AI governance relationship</div><h2 id=\"comparison-title\" class=\"section-heading medium\">A different question from the AI governance layer</h2><p class=\"section-lede\">AI governance platforms such as Credo AI and IBM watsonx.governance are built to answer whether an AI system is tested, monitored and compliant, and both describe themselves that way. MIZAN does not compete with that layer. It starts from its output and asks whether the institution is currently entitled to rely on it for one specific use.</p><div class=\"comparison-wrap\"><table class=\"comparison-table\"><thead><tr><th>Platform</th><th>What they say about themselves</th><th>What they track</th><th>The question they answer</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a class=\"inline-link\" href=\"https://www.credo.ai/\">Credo AI</a></td><td>\"AI Governance, Built for the Agentic Era\" and \"Measurable Trust for Every AI System\"</td><td>The AI system, agent, model and vendor</td><td>Is this AI trustworthy and under policy control?</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"inline-link\" href=\"https://www.ibm.com/products/watsonx-governance\">IBM watsonx.governance</a></td><td>\"Govern smarter. Scale faster.\" and \"Continuous accountability\"</td><td>The AI use case, across its lifecycle</td><td>Is this AI documented, monitored and compliant?</td></tr><tr class=\"mizan-row\"><td><strong>MIZAN</strong></td><td>\"Clear, accountable decisions about AI use\"</td><td>The institution's permission to use it, for this specific case</td><td>Is this institution entitled, right now, to let this AI act?</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"source-note\">Quoted from each platform's own public homepage or product page, fetched 30 September 2026. Shown for factual comparison only, not as a ranking. MIZAN is designed to complement AI governance and assurance tools, not replace them.</p></div></section>\n      <section class=\"section light\" aria-labelledby=\"architecture-title\"><div class=\"container\"><div class=\"section-kicker\">How the record is assembled</div><h2 id=\"architecture-title\" class=\"section-heading medium\">Evidence and approval flow into one maintained record</h2><div class=\"architecture-flow\"><article><span>01</span><h3>Policy</h3><p>Applicable rules, public purpose and operating constraints.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Capability</h3><p>Institutional readiness, people, supervision and escalation.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>System assurance</h3><p>Tests, privacy, security and operational evidence.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Authorisation</h3><p>Named decision, conditions and review date.</p></article></div><div class=\"hero-actions\"><a class=\"button secondary\" href=\"/how-it-works/\">See the full workflow</a></div></div></section>"
  },
